/-!
# Powers of an ideal sheaf as a coherent module, and the resolution property applied to them

Let `X` be a locally Noetherian scheme and `I` a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on `X`. The
subsheaf `Iⁿ ⊆ 𝒪_X` is a quasi-coherent submodule of the structure sheaf, hence coherent, hence
of finite type; so if `X` has the resolution property there is a finite locally free module
surjecting onto `Iⁿ`. That surjection is the input
`𝓔 → 𝓘` of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FZ0], in the form in which the class
`AlgebraicGeometry.HasResolutionProperty` can supply it: the class produces a quotient of a
*given* finite type quasi-coherent module, so what has to be checked is that a power of an ideal
sheaf is such a module.

Taking the power of the ideal sheaf before applying the resolution property removes the tensor
powers from the argument of the source: there `𝓔 → 𝓘` is chosen first and
`𝓔^{⊗ n} → 𝓘ⁿ` is deduced, whereas a surjection onto `𝓘ⁿ` is already available directly.

The file also computes the ideal of a power of the product ideal sheaf
`𝓙 = pr₁^*𝓘 · pr₂^*𝓘'` of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.externalProduct` on an
affine open of `X ×_S Y` lying over affine opens of `X` and of `Y`: it is the product of the
ideals generated by the images of `𝓘(U)ⁿ` and of `𝓘'(V)ⁿ`. This is the affine-local form of
the identification of `𝓙` with the image of
`pr₁^*𝓘 ⊗ pr₂^*𝓘' → 𝒪_{X ×_S Y}` that the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FZ0] uses, and it is what
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_externalProduct_eq_compl` leaves open.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_comap_of_isAffineOpen`: for an arbitrary
  morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` and affine opens `U ⊆ Y`, `V ⊆ f⁻¹ U`, the ideal of `I.comap f` on `V`
  is generated by the image of the ideal of `I` on `U`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_externalProduct_pow`: the ideal of `𝓙ⁿ` on an
  affine open of the fibre product lying over affine opens of the two factors.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit.obj_idealPow_externalProduct_affineOpen`: the same
  computation read as the sections of `𝓙ⁿ` viewed as a sheaf of modules.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isCoherent_idealPow`: a power of a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on a
  locally Noetherian scheme is coherent.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_epi_idealPow`: on a locally Noetherian scheme
  with the resolution property, every power of a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals is a quotient of
  a finite locally free module.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_of_isAffineHom` computes the ideal of an inverse image ideal
sheaf on the preimage of an affine open, for an *affine* morphism. Affineness enters there only
to make that preimage affine, so that the restricted morphism is a morphism of affine schemes;
if instead an affine open `V` contained in the preimage is given, the restriction
`Scheme.Hom.resLE` to `V` is a morphism of affine schemes for every `f`, and the same argument
applies verbatim. That is `ideal_comap_of_isAffineOpen`, which is the form needed on a fibre
product, where neither projection is affine.

The coherence of `Iⁿ` is [Stacks, Tag 01Y1] applied to the inclusion `Iⁿ ⊆ 𝒪_X`: the structure
sheaf of a locally Noetherian scheme is coherent and `Iⁿ` is quasi-coherent. The inclusion is a
monomorphism by Mathlib's instance for `SheafOfModules.Submodule.ι`, which is stated in
`SheafOfModules`; `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` is a `def` for that category and copies its
category instance, so the two `Mono` propositions are not syntactically the same.
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.mono_submodule_ι` is the declaration at the `X.Modules`
spelling, and this file uses it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FZ0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FZ0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Y1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Y1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F86](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F86)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData

/-! ### The inverse image of an ideal sheaf on an affine open of the source -/

/-- **The inverse image of an ideal sheaf, on an affine open of the source.** For any morphism
`f : X ⟶ Y`, an affine open `U` of `Y` and an affine open `V` of `X` contained in `f⁻¹ U`, the
ideal of `I.comap f` on `V` is generated by the image of the ideal of `I` on `U`.

`Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_of_isAffineHom` is the case `V = f⁻¹ U`, which needs `f` affine
for `f⁻¹ U` to be affine. No affineness of `f` is needed once `V` is given: the restriction
`f.resLE U V` is a morphism of affine schemes, so
`Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_top_of_isAffine` applies to it. -/
theorem ideal_comap_of_isAffineOpen {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Y.IdealSheafData) (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (U : Y.affineOpens) (V : X.affineOpens) (e : V.1 ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :
    (I.comap f).ideal V = Ideal.map (f.appLE U.1 V.1 e).hom (I.ideal U) := by
  have hU : IsAffine U.1.toScheme := U.2
  have hV : IsAffine V.1.toScheme := V.2
  have hgtop : (f.resLE U.1 V.1 e).appTop =
      U.1.topIso.hom ≫ f.appLE U.1 V.1 e ≫ V.1.topIso.inv := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.appTop, Scheme.Hom.resLE_app_top]
  have hcomap : (I.comap U.1.ι).comap (f.resLE U.1 V.1 e) = (I.comap f).comap V.1.ι := by
    rw [← comap_comp, ← comap_comp, Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι]
  have key := Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_top_of_isAffine (I.comap U.1.ι)
    (f.resLE U.1 V.1 e)
  have e1 : ((I.comap U.1.ι).comap (f.resLE U.1 V.1 e)).ideal
        ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top V.1.toScheme⟩ =
      Ideal.map V.1.topIso.inv.hom ((I.comap f).ideal V) :=
    (congrArg (fun K : V.1.toScheme.IdealSheafData ↦
        K.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top V.1.toScheme⟩) hcomap).trans
      (Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_ι_top (I.comap f) V.2 _)
  have e2 : (I.comap U.1.ι).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top U.1.toScheme⟩ =
      Ideal.map U.1.topIso.inv.hom (I.ideal U) :=
    Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_ι_top I U.2 _
  have main : Ideal.map V.1.topIso.inv.hom ((I.comap f).ideal V) =
      Ideal.map V.1.topIso.inv.hom (Ideal.map (f.appLE U.1 V.1 e).hom (I.ideal U)) := by
    rw [← e1, key, e2, Ideal.map_map, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp, hgtop, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc,
      CommRingCat.hom_comp, ← Ideal.map_map]
  exact Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_map_hom_injective V.1.topIso.symm main

/-! ### The product ideal sheaf on an affine open of the fibre product -/

/-- **The ideal of `𝓙ⁿ` on an affine open of `X ×_S Y`.** If `W` is an affine open of the fibre
product contained in `pr₁⁻¹ U ⊓ pr₂⁻¹ V` for affine opens `U ⊆ X` and `V ⊆ Y`, then the ideal of
the `n`-th power of `𝓙 = pr₁^*𝓘 · pr₂^*𝓘'` on `W` is the product of the ideals generated by the
images of `𝓘(U)ⁿ` and of `𝓘'(V)ⁿ`.

This is the affine-local form of the description of `𝓙` as the image of
`pr₁^*𝓘 ⊗ pr₂^*𝓘' → 𝒪_{X ×_S Y}`: on `W` the ideal is generated by the products of pullbacks of
sections of `𝓘ⁿ` and of `𝓘'ⁿ`. -/
theorem ideal_externalProduct_pow {X Y S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (g : Y ⟶ S)
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (I' : Y.IdealSheafData) (n : ℕ)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (V : Y.affineOpens) (W : (pullback f g).affineOpens)
    (hU : W.1 ≤ pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) (hV : W.1 ≤ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ V.1) :
    ((externalProduct f g I I') ^ n).ideal W =
      Ideal.map ((pullback.fst f g).appLE U.1 W.1 hU).hom (I.ideal U ^ n) *
        Ideal.map ((pullback.snd f g).appLE V.1 W.1 hV).hom (I'.ideal V ^ n) := by
  have h1 : ((externalProduct f g I I') ^ n).ideal W
      = ((I.comap (pullback.fst f g)).ideal W * (I'.comap (pullback.snd f g)).ideal W) ^ n := by
    simp [externalProduct]
  rw [h1, ideal_comap_of_isAffineOpen I (pullback.fst f g) U W hU,
    ideal_comap_of_isAffineOpen I' (pullback.snd f g) V W hV, mul_pow,
    ← Ideal.map_pow, ← Ideal.map_pow]

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit

/-- **The sections of `𝓙ⁿ` as a sheaf of modules, on an affine open of `X ×_S Y`.** The
submodule of `𝒪_{X ×_S Y}(W)` cut out by `idealPow (externalProduct f g I I') n` is the product
of the ideals generated by the images of `𝓘(U)ⁿ` and of `𝓘'(V)ⁿ`, for `W` an affine open
contained in `pr₁⁻¹ U ⊓ pr₂⁻¹ V`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_externalProduct_pow` read through the
identification of the two encodings of a power of an ideal sheaf. -/
theorem obj_idealPow_externalProduct_affineOpen {X Y S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (g : Y ⟶ S)
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (I' : Y.IdealSheafData) (n : ℕ)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (V : Y.affineOpens) (W : (pullback f g).affineOpens)
    (hU : W.1 ≤ pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) (hV : W.1 ≤ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ V.1) :
    (idealPowerMultiple (Scheme.IdealSheafData.externalProduct f g I I') n
          (structureModule (pullback f g))).toSubmodule.obj (op W.1) =
      Ideal.map ((pullback.fst f g).appLE U.1 W.1 hU).hom (I.ideal U ^ n) *
        Ideal.map ((pullback.snd f g).appLE V.1 W.1 hV).hom (I'.ideal V ^ n) :=
  (obj_idealPow_affineOpen_eq_ideal_pow _ n W).trans
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_externalProduct_pow f g I I' n U V W hU hV)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **A power of a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on a locally Noetherian scheme is coherent.**
It is a quasi-coherent submodule of the structure sheaf, which is itself coherent, so
[Stacks, Tag 01Y1] applies. -/
theorem isCoherent_idealPow [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (I : X.IdealSheafData) (n : ℕ) :
    (idealPow I n).IsCoherent := by
  have h1 : (idealPow I n).IsQuasicoherent := inferInstance
  refine @Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentSubquotients.isCoherent_of_mono X _
    (structureModule X) (idealPow I n) ?_ h1
    (idealPowerMultiple I n (structureModule X)).ι
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.mono_submodule_ι (idealPowerMultiple I n (structureModule X)))
  infer_instance

/-- **The resolution property applied to a power of an ideal sheaf.** On a locally Noetherian
scheme with the resolution property, every power of a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals is the
target of an epimorphism from a finite locally free module.

This is the input `𝓔 → 𝓘ⁿ` of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FZ0].
`AlgebraicGeometry.HasResolutionProperty` produces a quotient of a given finite type
quasi-coherent module, and `isCoherent_idealPow` is what says that `𝓘ⁿ` is one. -/
theorem exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_epi_idealPow [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [HasResolutionProperty X] (I : X.IdealSheafData) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ (E : X.Modules) (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := X.ringCatSheaf) E)
      (q : E ⟶ idealPow I n), Epi q := by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ :=
    @Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.isQuasicoherent_isFiniteType_of_isCoherent
      X (idealPow I n) (isCoherent_idealPow I n)
  exact @HasResolutionProperty.exists_finiteLocallyFree_quotient X _ (idealPow I n) h1 h2

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
